 4. Training data 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Democrats still lack a meaningful AI strategy . (Axios) Amazon is said to be planning an off-grid, gas-powered data center in Texas that could emit more carbon dioxide than any power plant in the country. (NYT) Meanwhile, the number of bans on new data centers in the U.S. now tops 500, per The Information. In Australia, a user's OpenClaw agent found flaws in a gym reservation system enabling the user to move up the waitlist by kicking off another user. (ABC News Australia) 
 
